Barreda Park of Legends (Spanish: Parque de las Leyendas \"Dr. Felipe Benavides Barreda\"), is a zoo located in San Miguel District, Lima, Peru.","wpu":"Parque de las Leyendas","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Vicu%C3%B1as_-_14386628680.jpg/960px-Vicu%C3%B1as_-_14386628680.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Huaca Casa Rosada","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-12.081667,"lo":-77.0875,"d":7654,"ds":"Huaca Casa Rosada is an archaeological site located in San Miguel District, in Lima, Peru, which occupies a total of 5300 square meters in the current urban area. The site presents evidence of human occupation from the Intermediate period to the Inca period and remains from the Spanish colonial and Republican periods.","wpu":"Huaca Casa Rosada","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/HuacaCasaRosada.jpg/960px-HuacaCasaRosada.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"El Frontón","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-12.116667,"lo":-77.181667,"d":8173,"ds":"El Frontón is a deserted island and former penal colony off the coast of Callao, Peru.","wpu":"El Frontón","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Las_ruinas_del_Front%C3%B3n_2013-04-04_06-58.jpg/960px-Las_ruinas_del_Front%C3%B3n_2013-04-04_06-58.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Larco Museum","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-12.072496,"lo":-77.070862,"d":8961,"ds":"The Larco Museum (officially known as Rafael Larco Herrera Archaeological Museum, in Spanish: Museo Arqueológico Rafael Larco Herrera) is a privately owned museum of pre-Columbian art, located in the Pueblo Libre district of Lima, Peru. The museum is housed in an 18th-century vice-royal building. It showcases chronological galleries that provide a thorough overview of 5,000 years of Peruvian pre-Columbian history.","wpu":"Larco Museum","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Lima_museo_larco.jpg/960px-Lima_museo_larco.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"San Lorenzo Island (Peru)","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-12.096389,"lo":-77.220833,"d":9269,"ds":"San Lorenzo is an island located in the Pacific Ocean off the coast of Callao, Peru. With an area of 16.48 square kilometres (6.36 sq mi), it is the largest island in the country. The island lacks natural sources of fresh water and remains uninhabited, although it currently houses a naval base of the Peruvian Navy.","wpu":"San Lorenzo Island (Peru)","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Isla_San_Lorenzo_-_ISS034-E-49361_%28cropped%29.JPG/960px-Isla_San_Lorenzo_-_ISS034-E-49361_%28cropped%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Church of the Immaculate Heart of Mary (Lima)","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-12.08691,"lo":-77.06895,"d":9721,"ds":"The Church of the Immaculate Heart of Mary (Spanish: Iglesia del Inmaculado Corazón de María), commonly known as The Dome (Spanish: La Cúpula), is a Catholic church located in the intersection of Antonio José de Sucre Avenue and Jirón 28 de Julio, in Magdalena del Mar District, Lima, Peru. The work was conceived by the Claretian priest Simón Llobet.","wpu":"Church of the Immaculate Heart of Mary (Lima)","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Iglesia_del_Inmaculado_Coraz%C3%B3n_de_Mar%C3%ADa_%28Lima%29_%2818_de_marzo%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/960px-Iglesia_del_Inmaculado_Coraz%C3%B3n_de_Mar%C3%ADa_%28Lima%29_%2818_de_marzo%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Mosque of Lima","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-12.0938,"lo":-77.0721,"d":9770,"ds":"The Mosque of Lima (Spanish: Mezquita de Lima), also known as the Mosque of Magdalena del Mar, is a mosque in Lima, Peru. It was erected in the areas of a mansion in 1986 by the Palestinian community in the city's Magdalena del Mar district. The mosque is open to the general public.","wpu":"Mosque of Lima","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Mezquita_de_Magdalena_-_Patio_01.jpg/960px-Mezquita_de_Magdalena_-_Patio_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"San Lorenzo Megaport Project","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-12.060556,"lo":-77.239722,"d":9826,"ds":"The San Lorenzo Megaport Project is a proposed plan to build a huge air, naval, and terrestrial port on the island of San Lorenzo in Callao, Peru using land reclamation techniques. It plans to be the largest port and only megaport in Latin America. The island is strategically located on the middle west coast of South America where it has easy access to Asia, North America, and Oceania.","wpu":"San Lorenzo Megaport Project","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/78/Peru.Lima.1889.Detalle.Stieler.png/960px-Peru.Lima.1889.Detalle.Stieler.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Flag Square, Lima","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-12.0675,"lo":-77.0612,"d":9850,"ds":"The Flag Square (Spanish: Plaza de la Bandera) is a public square in Lima, Peru. It is located next to the Mateo Salado Huaca at the intersection of Breña, Lima and Pueblo Libre districts.","wpu":"Flag Square, Lima","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/MINISTRO_DE_DEFENSA_PRESIDI%C3%93_CEREMONIA_POR_EL_199_ANIVERSARIO_DE_CREACI%C3%93N_DE_LA_PRIMERA_BANDERA_DEL_PER%C3%9A.jpg/960px-MINISTRO_DE_DEFENSA_PRESIDI%C3%93_CEREMONIA_POR_EL_199_ANIVERSARIO_DE_CREACI%C3%93N_DE_LA_PRIMERA_BANDERA_DEL_PER%C3%9A.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Church of Santa María Magdalena (Lima)","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-12.07817,"lo":-77.06337,"d":9927,"ds":"The Church of Saint Mary Magdalene (Spanish: Iglesia de Santa María Magdalena) is a Catholic church under the ecclesiastical jurisdiction of the Archdiocese of Lima, located at Avenida San Martin 1138, in the district of Pueblo Libre, Lima, Peru. It was declared Cultural Heritage of the Nation in 1942 by resolution LN° 9599.","wpu":"Church of Santa María Magdalena (Lima)","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/MariaMagdalena0001.jpg/960px-MariaMagdalena0001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Monument to the Immaculate Heart of Mary","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-12.0973,"lo":-77.07208,"d":9972,"ds":"The Monument to the Immaculate Heart of Mary (Spanish: Monumento al Inmaculado Corazón de María) is a monument in Magdalena del Mar District, Lima, Peru.","wpu":"Monument to the Immaculate Heart of Mary","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Monumento_de_la_Virgen_del_Inmaculado_Coraz%C3%B3n_de_Mar%C3%ADa_%281%29.jpg/960px-Monumento_de_la_Virgen_del_Inmaculado_Coraz%C3%B3n_de_Mar%C3%ADa_%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"}],"about":{"ds":"Lima is the capital and largest city of Peru, as well as a primate city. It is located in the valleys of the Chillón, Rímac and Lurín Rivers, in the desert zone of the central coastal part of the country, overlooking the Pacific Ocean. The city is considered the political, cultural, financial and commercial center of Peru.","wpu":"Lima","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/Bas%C3%ADlica_Catedral_Metropolitana_de_Lima_%28cropped%29.jpg/960px-Bas%C3%ADlica_Catedral_Metropolitana_de_Lima_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},"wk":"2026-10-18"}